[Round 8/8 | Implementer | 607.3s | 0/400k] The first benchmark run showed the optimistic scan itself is now the dominant cost (about 4.1–4.9M ops/s), despite correctness probes passing. I’m reducing summary metadata to the minimum needed for sound publication visibility—an acquire/release nonempty flag plus an atomic root priority—and keeping the heap-root revalidation under the selected shard lock. I also retain per-consumer rotated tie selection so equal priorities do not funnel every consumer into shard zero.

