[Round 8/8 | Implementer | 1180.6s | 0/400k] The benchmark variance is large, but the hot scan still performs two atomics per shard even though the normal benchmark priorities are not `u64::MAX`. I’m switching the summary to a single atomic priority word with an explicit rare-case marker for a real `u64::MAX` root; empty is encoded as the same word plus marker=false, so arbitrary priorities remain supported while normal dequeue scans one atomic per shard.

