[Round 8/8 | Implementer | 115.8s | 0/400k] The current M5 slice has two concrete correctness hazards: its root summary stores “priority” and “present” separately, and its dequeue validation relies on snapshots that can go stale across shards. I’m replacing that with a synchronized seqlock summary plus a queue-wide publication epoch used only for validation/retry, while keeping enqueue mutations on one shard lock and avoiding a global publication mutex.

