[Round 8/8 | Implementer | 909.7s | 0/400k] The exact-entry version counter is not needed for priority correctness when the root changes only among equal-priority entries; equal-priority order is explicitly arbitrary. Removing that extra selected-shard atomic check and retaining priority revalidation materially improved the short MPMC median (about 7.0M in the latest three-sample run). The shard root summaries still use their seqlock to validate concurrent cross-shard observations, and I’m keeping the longer official-style measurement on this faster path.

