[Round 8/8 | Judge | 409.0s | 0/400k] The higher-trial gate exposed a real correctness failure in SPSC at capacity 2. A dequeue removes its item from the publication heap but does not return the slot to the reservation pool until after payload copying and just before the call returns; an overlapping enqueue can therefore report `FULL` while the logical queue has only one published item. That history is not linearizable for SPSC/MPSC/SPMC, even though the reservation-aware MPMC model may permit the overlap. I’m recording the exact failing history and still checking the benchmark criterion.

